================================================================================

This Elixir implementation (DeepEvalEx) is based on the algorithms, metrics,
and evaluation patterns from the original DeepEval Python library. While the
code has been rewritten in Elixir to be idiomatic to the BEAM ecosystem, the
core evaluation logic, metric definitions, and prompt templates are derived
from the original work.

Key components derived from DeepEval:
- Evaluation metric algorithms (G-Eval, Faithfulness, Hallucination, etc.)
- Prompt templates for LLM-as-judge evaluation
- Test case and result data structures
- Metric scoring and aggregation logic

================================================================================

Verbatim prompt templates:

The judge prompts in lib/deep_eval_ex/prompts/ (answer_relevancy.ex,
contextual_precision.ex, contextual_recall.ex, faithfulness.ex, g_eval.ex,
hallucination.ex and tool_correctness.ex) contain text copied verbatim from
DeepEval 4.3.1's prompt templates (deepeval/metrics/*/templates/*.txt and
deepeval/templates/metrics/fragments/*.txt), Copyright 2023-2024 Confident
AI, licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0. The text is reproduced
unmodified so that DeepEvalEx sends the same prompts as DeepEval; only the
template placeholders were replaced with Elixir interpolation.

